---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const updated = '16 August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Anchor"
  description="Anchor collects nothing. No account, no analytics, no servers. Your focus history stays on your device and syncs only through your own private iCloud."
>
  <section class="hero" style="border-top: 0; padding-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 42px);">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Anchor has no servers, no account system and no analytics. There is no data for us to
      collect, because none of it ever reaches us.
    </p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What Anchor stores</h2>
    <p>
      Anchor stores the focus sessions you run and the distractions you write down: the goal,
      the intended and actual length, timestamps, the note you typed, and a category. This is
      written to a database on your device.
    </p>

    <h3>Where it goes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>On your device.</strong> The database lives in Anchor's own container on your
        Mac, iPhone or Apple Watch.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>In your iCloud, if you use it.</strong> When you're signed in to iCloud, Anchor
        syncs through Apple's CloudKit into your <em>private</em> database. That data is held in
        your Apple account under Apple's terms. We cannot see it, and we have no way to request
        it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Nowhere else.</strong> Anchor has no backend. It does not send your sessions,
        notes, categories, usage or device information to us or to any third party.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What Anchor does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No accounts, sign-ups, logins or email collection.</li>
      <li>No analytics, telemetry, crash reporting or usage measurement.</li>
      <li>No advertising, no advertising identifiers, no tracking across apps or websites.</li>
      <li>No third-party SDKs. Anchor is built only on Apple's frameworks.</li>
      <li>No selling or sharing of data — there is none to sell or share.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Apple Intelligence</h2>
    <p>
      Anchor uses Apple's on-device foundation model to group goals into themes and sort
      distractions into categories, and to write an optional one-paragraph summary of a period.
      This runs entirely on your device through Apple's Foundation Models framework. Your notes
      are not sent to Apple, to us, or to any cloud model.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where Apple Intelligence is unavailable — an ineligible device, the feature switched off,
      or on Apple Watch, where Apple ships no on-device model — Anchor falls back to built-in
      keyword rules that also run locally.
    </p>

    <h2>The MCP server</h2>
    <p>
      Anchor includes an optional local MCP server so an AI client on your own machine can query
      your focus history. It runs on your computer, reads the same local database, and is
      started only by a client you have configured yourself. Anchor does not transmit anything
      to run it. If you connect it to an AI client that itself sends data to a cloud service,
      that transfer is governed by that client's privacy policy, not this one.
    </p>

    <h2>Export</h2>
    <p>
      You can export your history to Excel, CSV or JSON at any time. Exported files go wherever
      you save them, and are then yours to handle.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Deleting the app removes its local database. To remove synced copies, delete Anchor's data
      from iCloud in your device settings. Because we hold nothing, there is no deletion request
      to send us.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Anchor is not directed at children under 13 and collects no personal information from
      anyone, of any age.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the revised version will be posted here with a new date. Anchor's
      posture — no collection, no servers — is a design decision, not a temporary state.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@significanthobbies.com">hello@significanthobbies.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
